  "_note": "P31.5 shadow-diff golden: the content digest (db.claim_sink.content_digest) of every record the connectors emit over the partner fixture set (tests/partner_fixtures.py), computed at the P31.5 base commit 34406ff, before the partner entity-ref claims existed. tests/connectors/test_partner_refs_shadow.py asserts the post-P31.5 records without an object_ref are exactly these. P32.3 (ADR-122): dot_511_wa re-goldened \u2014 the registry agency label now emits camera_registry_publisher (provenance) instead of camera_operator; WA has no authoritative operator field so no operator claims mint. P35.9 (ACQ-05): usaspending_awards re-goldened \u2014 award claims now carry the sweep-slice provenance fields (slice/index_keyword/agency/recipient_search/program_number/acq_keyword_terms) in evidence, and the person-shaped fixture recipient (SIG-FIXTURE-A-002 'JOHN Q CITIZEN') emits no recipient claim at all \u2014 the P8-6 recipient drop, recorded as recipient_dropped=person_shaped on the notice row and recipient_dropped_count=1 on the slice outcome row. P35.15a (PKG-07, F-329/F-523): dot_511_wa re-goldened \u2014 each camera-registry subject now emits a `technology` claim carrying the target's declared SKOS slug (fixed-camera-ptz) and the entity row's record_kind IS that declared subtype instead of the blanket `traffic_camera` literal; the dot_511 vocab_version stamp (2026.10.11.1) normalizes back to the golden-era 2026.10.10.1 via GOLDEN_DOT511_VOCAB. P35.66 (SIG-PUB-005/013): dot_511_wa re-goldened \u2014 every emitted entity and claim row now carries the residential-parcel screen stamps (residential_parcel_flag, parcel_screen, parcel_screen_signal); the committed declared signal has empty coverage so every record reads parcel_screen=unscreened. The dot_511 vocab_version stamp (2026.10.12.3) still normalizes back to 2026.10.10.1 via GOLDEN_DOT511_VOCAB.",
